# gopls may exit after `exit` with a frame's header written and its body not: F1 then fails on
# what it saw, and J1, J5, J7 and K2 are inconclusive about that frame. Seen in CI, and in 2 of 3
# local runs of K2's baseline (2026-11-09). With no body, no message can have been in it, so the
# checks that ask only whether output was missed (J3, K1, M3) aren't affected.
F1 pass|fail
F2 pass
F3 pass
F4 pass
F5 pass
F6 pass
F7 pass
F8 pass
J1 pass|error
J2 fail
J3 pass
J4 pass
J5 pass|error
J6 pass
J7 pass|error
L1 fail
L2 pass
L3 pass
L4 pass
L5 fail
L6 pass
L7 pass
L8 pass
L9 pass
C1 pass
C2 pass
C3 pass
# gopls publishes diagnostics for only some versions of a changed document. In the mutation scenario its only
# informative D1 positions are in the publish for case 3's version 10: D1 passes when that publish is read
# before the next version is sent, and is not-exercised when gopls publishes nothing for that version. Both
# verdicts are right for what lspcheck saw, and LSP doesn't require a publish for every version. Seen in one of
# four local runs of 10 cases, the one under load (2026-11-15).
D1 pass|not-exercised
D2 pass
D3 not-exercised
D4 pass
D5 not-exercised
D6 pass
K1 pass
K2 pass|error
R1 fail
R2 pass
R3 pass
R4 fail
M1 pass
M2 pass
M3 pass
